## The Recall Report: A Snapshot

This year has seen an alarming 543 recalls, pushing the all-time total past the 900 mark. The breakdown is concerning: 173 Class I recalls, 334 Class II recalls, and 36 Class III recalls--each a marker of risk severity.

To put things into perspective, 86 cases involve repeat offenders. These are brands that have been previously flagged for similar safety violations. Among these, Moonlight Packing Corporation leads the hall of shame with 96 recall points, followed closely by Ghirardelli Chocolate Company and Albertsons Companies LLC.

## Recent Highlights

On June 10th, multiple recalls were reported due to contamination and mislabeling. Notable cases include:

- *J and J Bunting, Inc*: Lunds & Byerly's Curry Powder Sweet labeled incorrectly.
- *Straus Family Creamery*: Metal pieces found in their premium ice creams.
- *JCB Flavors, LLC*: Salmonella contamination across several seasoning products.
- *Market of Choice Inc*: Undeclared sesame allergen in Vegan Kale Caesar Salad.

## The Monthly Breakdown

May 2026 peaked with 173 recalls. June showed a drop to 43 so far, but the trend signals a year far from average when it comes to food safety. Over 256 cases this year involved allergens, and 172 were linked to Salmonella, highlighting persistent issues despite regulation efforts.

## What's Next?

As investigations continue, it becomes clear that addressing the root causes of these recalls is crucial. From mislabeling to contamination, every case suggests lapses in oversight and quality control. For frequent offenders, stricter penalties may be inevitable.

## Should You Be Concerned?

The answer is nuanced. While the recall system serves as a safeguard, the consistency of certain brands appearing in these reports hints at deeper issues. Shoppers should remain informed, especially about brands with a poor track record.
